.SH "NAME"
whawty-nginx-sso \- simple SSO system for nginx
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR \fI[global options]\fR \fB<command>\fR \fI[command options]\fR \fI[arguments \&... ]\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
\fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR is a simple agent that can be used to implement a cookie\-based SSO scheme for the web\&. For this purpose the agent hosts a login form to prompt users for login credentials\&. These credentials are then verified using the configured authentication backend and in case they match a session cookie will be generated\&. The cookie is signed using an asymmetric signature algorithm and can whence be verfied by other \fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR instances which don\(cqt need to have access to the private signing key\&. To control the access to services the \fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR agent offers a endpoint intended to be used with the ngx_http_auth_request_module\&. Depending on the cookie options configured the session\- cookies generated can be used for all services of a given domain\&. Even if those services are hosted by different machines as long as they are published by nginx\&. Either directly or in the form of a reverse\-proxy\&.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following global options can be passed to \fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR\&.
.PP
\fB\-h | \-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Show help text and exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-v | \-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit\&.
.RE
.SH "COMMANDS"
.sp
Any of the following commands supports \fB\-h | \-\-help\fR as an option\&. This will print extra help information for the command\&.
.SS "run"
.sp
Runs the \fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR agent as configured by the global configuration file\&. This command has no command\-specific options
.SH "WEB INTERFACE"
.sp
The web interface and the endpoints for nginx are served on the address configured with \fBweb\&.listen\fR\&. All of them are mounted under \fBweb\&.base\-path\fR, which defaults to \fI/\fR\&. Only the prometheus endpoint uses the path configured for it as is\&.
.PP
\fB<base\-path>/login\fR
.RS 4
The login form, or the list of sessions of the user if the request carries a valid session cookie\&. The query parameter
\fBredir\fR
says where to send users after logging in\&. Users who are logged in already are sent there right away, i\&.e\&. when they reload a login form they opened before logging in elsewhere\&. A service which doesn\(cqt accept the session (because of a misconfiguration) sends them straight back, browsers stop such redirect loops\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB<base\-path>/logout\fR
.RS 4
Logs users out of the session of the request and sends them to the query parameter
\fBredir\fR
or the login form\&. Other sessions of the user can be revoked using a POST request with the session ID in the form field
\fBid\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB<base\-path>/auth\fR
.RS 4
The endpoint for the ngx_http_auth_request_module\&. It answers requests with a valid session cookie with status 200 and the username in the header
\fBX\-Username\fR, all others with 401\&. If nginx passes on the URI of the original request in the header
\fBX\-Origin\-URI\fR
the 401 answers contain the header
\fBX\-Login\-Redir\fR
with the URL of the original request, escaped for use as query parameter
\fBredir\fR
of the login form (nginx can\(cqt do that itself)\&. The URL is absolute if nginx also passes on the headers
\fBX\-Host\fR
and
\fBX\-Forwarded\-Proto\fR, otherwise it is just the path\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB<base\-path>/sessions\fR
.RS 4
The sessions of the user of the request as JSON\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB<base\-path>/revocations\fR
.RS 4
The revoked sessions for other instances, see
\fBcookie\&.backend\&.sync\fR\&. Requests must carry one of the tokens configured in
\fBweb\&.revocations\&.tokens\fR
as bearer token\&.
.RE
.sp
Users are only sent on to paths on the same host and to http(s) URLs of hosts which get the session cookie: the cookie domain (\fBcookie\&.domain\fR) and its subdomains, or the host the request was sent to if no cookie domain is configured\&. Other targets are ignored\&.
.sp
All links and redirects of the web interface are relative\&. If a reverse proxy strips a path prefix before passing requests on, leave \fBweb\&.base\-path\fR unset\&. Set it if the proxy passes the prefix on, i\&.e\&. for nginx \fIlocation /sso/ { proxy_pass \fR\fIhttp://127\&.0\&.0\&.1:1234\fR\fI; }\fR and \fIweb\&.base\-path: /sso\fR\&. See contrib/nginx\-vhost and contrib/nginx\-shared\-vhost for examples\&.
.sp
Form posts which other sites make on behalf of users are rejected\&. Browsers which don\(cqt send the header Sec\-Fetch\-Site are checked by comparing the Origin header with the Host header, so the reverse proxy should pass the Host header on (for nginx \fIproxy_set_header Host $host;\fR)\&.
.sp
All responses carry a Content\-Security\-Policy which only allows styles and images of the web interface itself, no scripts at all and no inline styles\&. Forms may only be sent to the web interface, which may redirect to the cookie domain and its subdomains\&. The pages must not be embedded by other sites\&. Custom templates (see TEMPLATES) have to stay within these limits as well\&.
.sp
The colours of the web interface can be changed without rebuilding \fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR: the pages load \fI<base\-path>/ui/css/theme\&.css\fR last, which is empty, so the reverse proxy can serve a replacement for it\&. See the comment in ui/assets/css/theme\&.css of the sources for an example\&.
.SH "TEMPLATES"
.sp
\fBweb\&.login\&.templates\fR replaces the built\-in templates with the files login\&.htmpl and logged\-in\&.htmpl from the given directory\&. They are pongo2 templates (a syntax like the one of Django templates), the built\-in ones in ui/templates of the sources are a good starting point\&. Values are escaped automatically\&.
.sp
All links must be relative\&. The static files of the web interface are available below \fIui/\fR, i\&.e\&. \fIui/css/base\&.css\fR, \fIui/css/app\&.css\fR, \fIui/css/theme\&.css\fR, \fIui/img/favicon\&.svg\fR and the icons as \fI<svg><use href="ui/vendor/icons\&.svg#<icon>"/></svg>\fR\&. The login form is a POST request to \fIlogin\fR with the fields \fBusername\fR, \fBpassword\fR and \fBredirect\fR\&. Other sessions are revoked with POST requests to \fIlogout\fR with the field \fBid\fR, \fIlogout\fR logs out of the own session\&.
.sp
login\&.htmpl gets these values:
.PP
\fBlogin\&.Title\fR
.RS 4
The title configured with
\fBweb\&.login\&.title\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBredirect\fR
.RS 4
Where to send users after logging in, already checked to be safe\&. Put it into the field
\fBredirect\fR
of the form\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBredirect_host\fR
.RS 4
The host of
\fBredirect\fR
if it is a URL\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBcookie_domain\fR
.RS 4
The cookie domain, if one is configured\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBusername\fR
.RS 4
The username of a failed login attempt\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBalerts\fR
.RS 4
A list of errors to show\&. Each has
\fBHeading\fR,
\fBMessage\fR
and
\fBLevel\fR
(danger, warning, success or info),
\fBClass()\fR
returns the CSS class and
\fBIcon()\fR
the name of the icon for it\&.
.RE
.sp
logged\-in\&.htmpl gets \fBlogin\&.Title\fR, \fBcookie_domain\fR and \fBalerts\fR as well as:
.PP
\fBsession\fR
.RS 4
The session of the request with
\fBUsername\fR,
\fBID\fR,
\fBCreatedAt()\fR
and
\fBExpiresAt()\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBcurrent\fR
.RS 4
The same session including
\fBAgent\fR, the browser it was created with:
\fBAgent\&.Name\fR,
\fBAgent\&.OS\fR
and
\fBAgent\&.DeviceType\fR\&. It may be missing\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBothers\fR
.RS 4
The other sessions of the user, newest first, with the same values as
\fBcurrent\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
Besides the built\-in filters of pongo2 the templates can use \fBtimesince\fR and \fBtimeuntil\fR, which turn times into "2 hours ago" and "6 days from now", and \fBua_icon\fR: \fI{{ s\&.Agent|ua_icon:"Name" }}\fR is the name of the icon of the browser, "OS" and "DeviceType" work the same\&.
.SH "BUGS"
.sp
Most likely there are some bugs in \fBwhawty\-nginx\-sso\fR\&. If you find a bug, please let the developers know at http://github\&.com/whawty/nginx\-sso\&. Of course, pull requests are preferred\&.
